depends_on: none
scope: AEP-Components/trust-rings AEP-Components/admit-trust-floor/crate AEP-Components/evaluation-chain/crate AEP-Components/gap-capability-dimensions AEP-SDKs/typescript/dynaep/src/protocol/action-lattice.ts AEP-Components/dynAEP AEP-Base-Node/multi-base-node/crate AEP-Components/workflow/lib/executor.ts AEP-User-Experience/AEP-main-skill README.md CHANGELOG.md
notes: Closed. Trust Rings four-stage rank is not a product member. Who-may-do-what is GAP dimension Conjunction. Agent A may X. Agent B may Y. No rank. evaluation-chain step 2 is gap_capability. admit-trust-floor is retargeted to agent_may walls. client trust_tier is not compared to a node floor. multi-base-node uses isolation_class. Isolation is not a trust rank. skip does not mutate trust during evaluation. CAW isolation stays. Out of scope: hangar tools.
architecture_operator: Trust Rings (sandbox < user < system < enterprise) are a hierarchy. Hierarchy is order. Order is what Envelope eliminates. Who-may-do-what is GAP dimension Conjunction. Isolation is not a trust rank.
acceptance: No sandbox < user < system < enterprise rank in product docs or code. No trust.penalize during Admit or evaluation. No client trust_tier floor compare. Who-may-do-what is GAP dimension Conjunction. evaluation-chain has no ring_capability step. trust-rings component is not a product member. Tests fail if a ring rank or penalize side effect remains on the live path. nla-policy-scan gate coding-completion and project-completion-bac on touched Rust crates before any ship prose.
